<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-415] Rename DeliveryThrottle to MessageWindowSize</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-415</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In hedwig server, DeliveryThrottle is a little inaccurate as it suggests that the rate is being limited, rather than a outstanding message limit being reached. I think MessageWindowSize is more accurate, and is analogous to windowing in tcp, which this mechanism actually replaces.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
